    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "A process is a running instance of a program. It has its own memory space, and the operating system keeps it separate from other processes.\n\nA thread is a path of execution inside a process. One process can have many threads. Threads in the same process share memory. Each thread has its own stack and its own register values.\n\nCreating a process costs more than creating a thread. Switching between threads is also faster than switching between processes.\n\nA crash in one process usually does not affect other processes. A crash in one thread can stop the whole process.\n\nThreads that share data need synchronization, such as locks. Processes need inter-process communication, such as pipes, sockets, or shared memory, to exchange data.",
